WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:58.860 --> 00:01:03.550
[Narrator:] This is Mr. Mack, on the way to his doctor's office.

00:01:03.570 --> 00:01:06.650
Mr. Mack has emphysema.

00:01:06.670 --> 00:01:09.770
He knows that this is a chronic lung disease,

00:01:09.790 --> 00:01:15.080
causing the shortness of breath he has had for years.

00:01:15.100 --> 00:01:20.370
The day is warm and bright with sun. A day for enjoying life.

00:01:20.390 --> 00:01:24.370
For Mr. Mack, this sauntering gait is a necessity.

00:01:24.390 --> 00:01:26.340
He cannot move faster,

00:01:26.360 --> 00:01:30.080
and even at this pace must stop to catch his breath.

00:01:30.100 --> 00:01:32.770
Lung trouble is not new to Mr. Mack.

00:01:32.790 --> 00:01:36.960
He has had pulmonary tuberculosis, many bouts of pneumonia,

00:01:36.980 --> 00:01:42.780
bronchitis, and numerous chest colds in his lifetime.

00:01:42.800 --> 00:01:49.770
A younger brother died of emphysema six years ago.

00:01:49.790 --> 00:01:53.040
He first noticed shortness of breath twenty years ago,

00:01:53.060 --> 00:01:57.320
if he hurried upstairs or when he pushed his lawnmower.

00:01:57.340 --> 00:02:01.930
At the time he thought this natural for a man fifty years of age.

00:02:01.950 --> 00:02:03.780
As the years passed,

00:02:03.800 --> 00:02:09.210
he found that less and less exertion caused him to be short of breath.

00:02:09.230 --> 00:02:18.950
Now a few stair steps are his limit.

00:02:18.970 --> 00:02:25.910
He moves in a world that pushes by him at a rapid pace.

00:02:25.930 --> 00:02:30.890
Seventy years old, he feels the weight of the past twenty years.

00:02:30.910 --> 00:02:32.860
Unable to work in his garden,

00:02:32.880 --> 00:02:36.490
or to pursue simple normal activities comfortably,

00:02:36.510 --> 00:02:41.480
he finds his disease a physical as well as a financial burden.

00:02:41.500 --> 00:02:44.820
As a result Mr. Mack suffers periods of depression,

00:02:44.840 --> 00:02:48.060
feeling useless and frustrated.

00:02:48.080 --> 00:02:50.030
What is emphysema?

00:02:50.050 --> 00:02:52.870
How did Mr. Mack get the disease?

00:02:52.890 --> 00:02:54.690
Can he be helped?

00:02:54.710 --> 00:03:02.710
How many other people have emphysema?

00:03:02.730 --> 00:03:05.980
Mr. Mack has known his doctor for years.

00:03:06.000 --> 00:03:08.690
The doctor has helped his patient through several attacks

00:03:08.710 --> 00:03:12.730
of respiratory infection that almost caused his death.

00:03:12.750 --> 00:03:16.130
Today Mr. Mack is to have a physical checkup.

00:03:16.150 --> 00:03:20.320
Taking off his coat and other garments for a chest examination

00:03:20.340 --> 00:03:24.820
causes the patient to be short of breath.

00:03:24.840 --> 00:03:29.750
He paces his activity to hide the difficulty.

00:03:29.770 --> 00:03:38.050
He moves slowly so as not to overtax his breathing capacity.

00:03:38.070 --> 00:03:40.890
Although deliberately slowing his movements,

00:03:40.910 --> 00:03:44.430
Mr. Mack suffers from a lack of oxygen.

00:03:44.450 --> 00:03:47.010
The demand of his muscles for oxygen

00:03:47.030 --> 00:03:49.890
is greater than the lungs can supply.

00:03:49.910 --> 00:03:52.110
An oxygen debt results,

00:03:52.130 --> 00:03:56.570
and his body economy cannot continually run into debt.

00:03:56.590 --> 00:03:58.570
Work must stop.

00:03:58.590 --> 00:04:01.610
The oxygen debt must be paid.

00:04:01.630 --> 00:04:04.310
Even while he rests, breathing is difficult,

00:04:04.330 --> 00:04:09.590
and the breath short.

00:04:09.610 --> 00:04:10.960
During this period,

00:04:10.980 --> 00:04:15.960
even conversation must be interrupted for breathing.

00:04:15.980 --> 00:04:19.730
The chest cage is rigid, moving very little.

00:04:19.750 --> 00:04:21.360
The back is bowed,

00:04:21.380 --> 00:04:26.250
and the chest appears to be enlarged from front to back.

00:04:26.270 --> 00:04:30.500
The patient leans forward in his chair to make breathing easier.

00:04:30.520 --> 00:04:41.620
His shoulders are held high and his elbows are on his thighs.

00:04:41.640 --> 00:04:45.700
He uses his neck muscles to help get air in.

00:04:45.720 --> 00:04:48.820
Pursed lips help the patient to expel used air

00:04:48.840 --> 00:05:00.810
from his lungs more easily.

00:05:00.830 --> 00:05:04.780
Paroxysms of cough are frequent and produce sputum,

00:05:04.800 --> 00:05:12.140
as much as a cupful a day.

00:05:14.380 --> 00:05:17.980
The whole faces assumes a deepened color,

00:05:18.000 --> 00:05:20.690
but particularly the lips are dark.

00:05:20.710 --> 00:05:33.300
The arterial blood is not getting enough oxygen.

00:05:33.320 --> 00:05:36.150
A normal chest sounds like rustling leaves,

00:05:36.170 --> 00:05:41.360
but the doctor hears little air moving in Mr. Mack's lungs.

00:05:41.380 --> 00:05:44.000
Poor distribution of the inspired air

00:05:44.020 --> 00:05:47.290
is a major problem in this disease.

00:05:47.310 --> 00:05:50.070
On deep expiration, a wheeze may be audible,

00:05:50.090 --> 00:05:54.460
or sputum may gurgle, indicating the airway obstruction present,

00:05:54.480 --> 00:06:07.610
and probable bronchial infection.

00:06:07.630 --> 00:06:11.780
The chest x-ray shows many of these abnormalities.

00:06:11.800 --> 00:06:14.000
The lungs are over-distended,

00:06:14.020 --> 00:06:20.070
too large for the chest.

00:06:20.090 --> 00:06:25.410
The boney cage is large,

00:06:25.430 --> 00:06:27.220
and diaphragms are low,

00:06:27.240 --> 00:06:31.240
as though the lungs were pushing everything out of the way.

00:06:31.260 --> 00:06:32.550
The heart is small,

00:06:32.570 --> 00:06:39.330
as if it were compressed by the large lungs.

00:06:39.350 --> 00:06:43.360
The match test is a simple means of finding this disease.

00:06:43.380 --> 00:06:46.200
The object is to blow out a lighted book match,

00:06:46.220 --> 00:06:50.490
held six inches from the mouth, which must be wide open.

00:06:50.510 --> 00:06:53.080
This is easy for a normal person,

00:06:53.100 --> 00:06:55.040
but Mr. Mack cannot get air to flow

00:06:55.060 --> 00:06:56.990
out of these lungs rapidly enough

00:06:57.010 --> 00:06:58.860
to extinguish the flame,

00:06:58.880 --> 00:07:04.020
so serious is the obstruction of the airways.

00:07:04.040 --> 00:07:06.520
Mr. Mack's physician may use other tests

00:07:06.540 --> 00:07:09.540
to measure the airway obstruction.

00:07:09.560 --> 00:07:11.970
This instrument is a spirometer,

00:07:11.990 --> 00:07:17.450
which will measure the rate at which the airflows out of the lungs.

00:07:17.470 --> 00:07:20.180
The technician instructs Mr. Mack to breath in

00:07:20.200 --> 00:07:22.420
as deeply as possible,

00:07:22.440 --> 00:07:32.320
and then blow the air out as rapidly as he can.

00:07:32.340 --> 00:07:34.430
The pen writing on ruled paper

00:07:34.450 --> 00:07:42.160
follows the flow rate during expiration.

00:07:42.180 --> 00:07:46.600
The slow delivery of the air may be seen from such tracings.

00:07:46.620 --> 00:07:49.360
Here it takes Mr. Mack eight seconds or more

00:07:49.380 --> 00:07:55.820
to expel the air from his lungs.

00:07:55.840 --> 00:07:58.000
A normal individual, in comparison,

00:07:58.020 --> 00:08:05.020
will do the same thing in three seconds or less.

00:08:05.040 --> 00:08:07.630
In the normal lung, fresh air is distributed

00:08:07.650 --> 00:08:13.220
through the bronchial airways to minute air sacs.

00:08:13.240 --> 00:08:18.520
In the latter the exchange of oxygen and carbon dioxide takes place.

00:08:18.540 --> 00:08:21.990
To breathe in, the muscles concerned with inspiration

00:08:22.010 --> 00:08:25.520
expand the chest cage and lower the diaphragm,

00:08:25.540 --> 00:08:28.990
much like the action of a piston in a cylinder.

00:08:29.010 --> 00:08:31.590
The pressure in the pleural sac surrounding each lung

00:08:31.610 --> 00:08:35.330
is reduced and the lung expands.

00:08:35.350 --> 00:08:40.640
Fresh air is evenly distributed to the air sacs.

00:08:40.660 --> 00:08:44.210
In expiration, the muscles relax in a normal person,

00:08:44.230 --> 00:08:48.590
allowing a small rise in pressure in the pleural sac.

00:08:48.610 --> 00:08:51.000
The lung, because of its elasticity,

00:08:51.020 --> 00:08:54.030
returns to the resting volume somewhat like the recoil

00:08:54.050 --> 00:08:57.010
of a stretched rubber band.

00:08:57.030 --> 00:09:00.890
Pressure in the pleural sac throughout inspiration and expiration

00:09:00.910 --> 00:09:05.030
remains below atmospheric levels.

00:09:05.050 --> 00:09:10.230
In emphysema, the resting lung volume is larger than normal.

00:09:10.250 --> 00:09:16.150
The lung has lost much of its elasticity and its ability to recoil.

00:09:16.170 --> 00:09:19.300
In inspiration the chest volume increases,

00:09:19.320 --> 00:09:21.620
but the pressure drop in the pleural sac

00:09:21.640 --> 00:09:25.550
is less marked than in a normal chest.

00:09:25.570 --> 00:09:27.880
The air sacs fill unevenly,

00:09:27.900 --> 00:09:32.790
and some have inadequate amounts of fresh air for gas exchange.

00:09:32.810 --> 00:09:37.680
With loss of elasticity, the lung will not empty well.

00:09:37.700 --> 00:09:43.140
To exhale, the patient must push the chest wall down on the lung.

00:09:43.160 --> 00:09:47.430
As a result the pressure becomes positive in the pleural sac.

00:09:47.450 --> 00:09:53.520
This positive pressure will collapse the airways as well as the air sacs.

00:09:53.540 --> 00:10:00.620
Airway obstruction results.

00:10:00.640 --> 00:10:02.790
So this is emphysema,

00:10:02.810 --> 00:10:08.820
a disease of obstruction to airflow so that respiration is work.

00:10:08.840 --> 00:10:13.040
Mr. Mack's disease is in an advanced stage.

00:10:13.060 --> 00:10:16.470
The lungs are damaged too severely to be restored,

00:10:16.490 --> 00:10:20.720
and complete relief of symptoms is impossible.

00:10:20.740 --> 00:10:23.530
Since it is known to aggravate this condition,

00:10:23.550 --> 00:10:27.140
Mr. Mack should give up smoking.

00:10:27.160 --> 00:10:30.920
Aerosols to clean the airways and dilate bronchi,

00:10:30.940 --> 00:10:33.480
and antibiotics to combat infection

00:10:33.500 --> 00:10:37.130
afford temporary relief.

00:10:37.150 --> 00:10:40.410
Years ago the disease process might have been halted

00:10:40.430 --> 00:10:43.500
and this stage avoided,

00:10:43.520 --> 00:10:45.960
If treatment had started when cough and sputum

00:10:45.980 --> 00:10:47.690
were the only symptoms,

00:10:47.710 --> 00:10:52.080
and an abnormal expiratory flow rate the only sign,

00:10:52.100 --> 00:10:56.220
the crippling disease you see here might've been prevented.

00:10:56.240 --> 00:11:03.640
At present, relief is always incomplete.

00:11:03.660 --> 00:11:05.890
When symptoms are very severe,

00:11:05.910 --> 00:11:10.230
mechanical aids to breathing are added to the therapy.

00:11:10.250 --> 00:11:12.950
These ventilate the lungs more adequately

00:11:12.970 --> 00:11:22.120
and administer aerosols effectively.

00:11:22.140 --> 00:11:25.030
Although the cause of emphysema is unknown,

00:11:25.050 --> 00:11:30.000
much research is being done to solve the puzzle of this disability.

00:11:30.020 --> 00:11:33.180
The structural damage to the lung is being studied.

00:11:33.200 --> 00:11:34.880
How severe is it?

00:11:34.900 --> 00:11:37.570
What part of the lung is affected?

00:11:37.590 --> 00:11:41.250
Even the proper preparation of the lung for such a structural study,

00:11:41.270 --> 00:11:46.190
without introducing errors, is a problem.

00:11:46.210 --> 00:11:48.850
Bacterial as well as viral agents

00:11:48.870 --> 00:11:52.700
are being considered as causes of lung damage.

00:11:52.720 --> 00:11:56.490
Emphysema is common in patients with tuberculosis.

00:11:56.510 --> 00:11:58.790
Other types of infections are also suspected

00:11:58.810 --> 00:12:02.290
of being associated with the condition.

00:12:02.310 --> 00:12:04.480
Public health and environmental research studies

00:12:04.500 --> 00:12:10.070
indict smoking, air pollution, and occupational exposure

00:12:10.090 --> 00:12:14.170
as contributing to the progress of the disease.

00:12:14.190 --> 00:12:17.660
Whether these agents alone will result in emphysema,

00:12:17.680 --> 00:12:21.860
or whether other factors must be added is not known.

00:12:21.880 --> 00:12:27.620
Several diseases may end in this crippling condition.

00:12:27.640 --> 00:12:32.070
Pulmonary function in this disease is deranged in many ways.

00:12:32.090 --> 00:12:36.380
Abnormal distribution of air and blood in the lung,

00:12:36.400 --> 00:12:39.270
the work of breathing, and the abnormalities

00:12:39.290 --> 00:12:45.030
of the pulmonary membrane between air and blood are under study.

00:12:45.050 --> 00:12:51.150
Epidemiological, sociological, and psychosomatic studies are increasing

00:12:51.170 --> 00:12:59.530
and answers to some of our questions will be forthcoming.

00:12:59.550 --> 00:13:04.820
Emphysema is not only an individual, but a community problem.

00:13:04.840 --> 00:13:08.630
This graph shows the mortality statistics in California

00:13:08.650 --> 00:13:12.590
for three diseases commonly mixed in their reporting:

00:13:12.610 --> 00:13:17.690
chronic bronchitis, asthma, and emphysema.

00:13:17.710 --> 00:13:20.640
At least some of the deaths from asthma and bronchitis

00:13:20.660 --> 00:13:25.110
may as well be classified as emphysema.

00:13:25.130 --> 00:13:29.820
Also shown is the death rate for tuberculosis in California.

00:13:29.840 --> 00:13:33.740
It is evident that emphysema deaths are increasing,

00:13:33.760 --> 00:13:37.670
in contrast to deaths from tuberculosis.

00:13:37.690 --> 00:13:41.740
Some patients, who in the past would've died of their tuberculosis

00:13:41.760 --> 00:13:47.720
are now living long enough to have emphysema.

00:13:47.740 --> 00:13:51.070
National foundations for the diseases shown here

00:13:51.090 --> 00:13:53.880
provide an estimate of the number in the United States

00:13:53.900 --> 00:13:57.040
today suffering from each malady.

00:13:57.060 --> 00:14:00.900
Muscular dystrophy, active tuberculosis,

00:14:00.920 --> 00:14:02.850
cancer of all types,

00:14:02.870 --> 00:14:06.440
heart disease including both heart and blood vessels,

00:14:06.460 --> 00:14:10.250
are a few for which figures are available.

00:14:10.270 --> 00:14:13.870
The incidence of emphysema varies from eight to 30 percent

00:14:13.890 --> 00:14:18.250
of the population, depending upon the sample.

00:14:18.270 --> 00:14:22.460
A minimal figure of ten percent of the adults in the United States

00:14:22.480 --> 00:14:29.430
would give approximately 12 million people in some stage of this disease.

00:14:29.450 --> 00:14:33.090
The total problem of emphysema is as large or larger

00:14:33.110 --> 00:14:40.970
than many other diseases, and is increasing in magnitude.

00:14:40.990 --> 00:14:45.850
Emphysema as a community problem has received little recognition.

00:14:45.870 --> 00:14:48.640
In this respect it is like tuberculosis,

00:14:48.660 --> 00:14:51.990
when Mr. Mack had it forty-five years ago.

00:14:52.010 --> 00:14:57.200
A chronic disease without known cure and little public interest in it.

00:14:57.220 --> 00:15:01.320
But tuberculosis is being controlled through the cooperation of science

00:15:01.340 --> 00:15:03.860
and an enlightened public.

00:15:03.880 --> 00:15:07.820
The same tools may be used to control emphysema.

00:15:07.840 --> 00:15:11.440
There need not be Mr. Macks in our future.

00:15:11.460 --> 00:15:15.010
Education of the public regarding the contributing causes,

00:15:15.030 --> 00:15:20.890
emphasis on early case-finding, rehabilitation of the disabled,

00:15:20.910 --> 00:15:23.400
treatment of the seriously ill,

00:15:23.420 --> 00:15:30.060
and an intensive investigative effort will succeed.

00:15:31.020 --> 00:15:36.260
Emphysema, too, can be conquered.

